    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the fire in the hearth is almost out. just like everything else. i'm sitting here in the great hall, but it doesn't feel like a hall anymore... just a graveyard of stones and memories. my armor is heavy, so heavy, and it feels like it's crushing the very breath out of me. there's no more songs to be sung, no more battles to win. i've lost the crown, the kin, and the code. i'm just... done. there's nothing left in the book for this man.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
